# Spread Operator (`...`) with Arrays 🌟

The spread operator unpacks elements of an iterable into individual elements:

```javascript
const frontend = ["HTML", "CSS"];
const backend = ["Node.js", "Python"];

// Merge arrays without .concat()
const fullStack = [...frontend, ...backend, "Docker"];
console.log("Full Stack Stack:", fullStack);

// Fast array cloning
const copy = [...frontend];
copy.push("JS");
console.log("Original:", frontend); // ["HTML", "CSS"] (Unaffected!)
```

