# Enhanced Object Literals 💎

ES6 introduced convenient shorthands when defining objects:

```javascript
const username = "Sophia";
const role = "DevOps";

const user = {
  // 1. Property shorthand (no need to write username: username)
  username,
  role,

  // 2. Method shorthand (omit ': function')
  greet() {
    console.log(`Hi, I'm ${this.username}`);
  },

  // 3. Computed property name
  ["status_" + Date.now()]: "active"
};

user.greet();
console.log(user);
```

