# Class Inheritance (`extends` and `super`) 🧬

Create child classes that inherit from parent classes:

```javascript
class User {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }
}

class Admin extends User {
  constructor(name, permissions) {
    super(name); // Calls parent constructor (MANDATORY!)
    this.permissions = permissions;
  }

  deleteUser(targetUser) {
    console.log(`${this.name} deleted ${targetUser.name}`);
  }
}

const admin = new Admin("Sarah", ["read", "write", "delete"]);
admin.deleteUser({ name: "Bob" });
```

