# Maps: Key-Value Collections with Any Key 🗺️

Unlike plain objects (which only allow string/symbol keys), a `Map` allows **any data type as a key** (including functions, objects, and numbers):

```javascript
const userRoles = new Map();

const userA = { id: 1 };
const userB = { id: 2 };

userRoles.set(userA, "SuperAdmin");
userRoles.set(userB, "Viewer");

console.log(userRoles.get(userA)); // "SuperAdmin"
console.log("Total entries in Map:", userRoles.size);
```

