# Private Class Fields (`#field`) 🔒

Modern ECMAScript provides truly private class fields prefixed with `#`:

```javascript
class Wallet {
  #balance = 0; // Private field!

  constructor(startingAmount) {
    this.#balance = startingAmount;
  }

  getBalance() {
    return this.#balance;
  }
}

const myWallet = new Wallet(500);
console.log("Balance:", myWallet.getBalance()); // 500
// console.log(myWallet.#balance); // SyntaxError: Private field '#balance' must be declared in an enclosing class!
```

