# Object.fromEntries: Inverse of Object.entries 🔄

Converts an iterable of key-value pairs back into a plain object:

```javascript
const entries = [["name", "Diana"], ["level", 42]];
const obj = Object.fromEntries(entries);

console.log(obj); // { name: "Diana", level: 42 }

// Transform object properties with map and fromEntries:
const prices = { apple: 1.5, orange: 2.0 };
const doubledPrices = Object.fromEntries(
  Object.entries(prices).map(([k, v]) => [k, v * 2])
);
console.log(doubledPrices); // { apple: 3.0, orange: 4.0 }
```

